        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ഗതാഗതം",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഗതാഗതം — gatāgataṁ — \"transport; traffic\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പുതിയ പാലം ഗതാഗതം എളുപ്പമാക്കി. putiya pālaṁ gatāgataṁ eḷuppamākki. The new bridge made transport easier."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A formal word for the movement of vehicles and people; it is common in the news."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഗതാഗതം (gatāgataṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit gatāgata, \"going and coming\" (Monier-Williams), a compound of gata, gone, and āgata, come."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
