          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വേഗത — vēgata — \"speed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇവിടെ വണ്ടികളുടെ വേഗത കുറവാണ്. iviṭe vaṇṭikaḷuṭe vēgata kuṟavāṇŭ. The speed of vehicles is low here."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വേഗം is quickness; വേഗത (vēgata) is speed as a measure. Fast is വേഗത്തിൽ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "വേഗത (vēgata) is built from Sanskrit vega, \"a rush, speed\" (Monier-Williams), with the ending -tā, which makes an abstract noun."
            }
